      "text": "| Concept | Explorer |\n|---------|---------|\n| First European account of China/Asia | Marco Polo (if accurate — disputed) |\n| Most widely traveled medieval explorer | Ibn Battuta |\n| Largest pre-modern naval expeditions | Zheng He |\n| Cape route to India | Vasco da Gama (1498) |\n| First European transatlantic voyage | Columbus (1492) |\n| Recognizing America as new continent | Vespucci (1499–1502) |\n| First circumnavigation (completed) | Elcano (Magellan died; 1522) |\n| Most scientific Pacific explorer | Cook (three voyages) |\n| Northwest Passage (first transit) | Amundsen (1903–06) |\n| South Pole (first) | Amundsen (1911) |\n| Greatest survival story in exploration | Shackleton (Endurance, 1914–16) |\n| First scientific natural history expedition | Humboldt (Americas, 1799–1804) |\n| Evolutionary theory origin (fieldwork) | Darwin (Beagle, 1831–36) |\n| Lewis and Clark expedition | Lewis + Clark (1804–06) |\n| First summit of Everest | Hillary + Tenzing (1953) |\n| All 14 eight-thousanders | Messner (1986) |\n| First human orbital spaceflight | Gagarin (1961) |\n| First Moon landing | Armstrong + Aldrin (1969) |\n| Deep ocean exploration | Cousteau; Ballard; Piccard |"
    },
